#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054384 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054654 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b170bf27-76bc-5558-9133-e81a4760072f" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Multiplication"}] :question/id #uuid "8955a3ce-a161-5dc5-8ec0-c357a0403b46" :question/math-academy-id "e-12862" :question/problem "Solve the equation $3p-7 =20$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding $7$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3p-7 &=20 \\\\ 3p-7+7 &=20+7 \\\\ 3p + 0 &= 27 \\\\ 3p &=27 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} 3p &=27 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{3p}{3} &=\\dfrac{27}{3} \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{\\cancel{3}p}{\\cancel{3}} &= 9 \\\\[5pt] p &=9 \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054385 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "52c2b31a-9b7a-52cb-9fa7-111de8bc53ea" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations while Keeping the Variable on the Right-Hand Side"}] :question/id #uuid "074b5213-4f4e-5d1b-a5c4-8b5403901b4d" :question/math-academy-id "e-12863" :question/problem "Solve for $x$ where $2=5x-8$." :question/worked-solution "To save time, we will keep the variable on the right-hand side as we solve. First, we apply the addition principle, adding $8$ to both sides:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2 &= 5x - 8 \\\\\n2 + 8 &= 5x - 8 + 8 \\\\\n10 &= 5x + 0 \\\\\n10 &= 5x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSecond, we apply the multiplication principle, dividing both sides by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10 &= 5x \\\\\n\\frac{10}{5} &= \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\\n2 &= \\frac{5x}{5} \\\\\n2 &= x\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $2=x$, we conclude that the solution is $x=2$."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054386 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ac53e171-0a02-5b74-8a3a-465dbecda9d7" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Division"}] :question/id #uuid "1f5b9030-a5de-5ac2-95c4-2fbaf638cdab" :question/math-academy-id "e-12864" :question/problem "Solve the equation $7-\\dfrac{p}{3} =9$." :question/worked-solution "After converting the equation to a more familiar form, we apply the addition principle, subtracting $7$ from both sides:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} 7-\\dfrac{p}{3} &=9 \\\\ -\\dfrac{p}{3}+7 &=9 \\\\ -\\dfrac{p}{3}+7-7 &= 9-7 \\\\ -\\dfrac{p}{3}+0 &= 2 \\\\ -\\dfrac{p}{3} &=2 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign, and again by $3$ to get rid of the fraction:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} -\\dfrac{p}{3} &=2 \\\\ (-1) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{p}{3} \\right) &=(-1) \\cdot 2 \\ \\dfrac{p}{3} &=-2 \\ \\cancel{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{p}{\\cancel{3}} &=3 \\cdot (-2) \\\\ p &=-6 \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054387 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82077653-3463-5132-b0a9-8376fdb47319" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Fractions"}] :question/id #uuid "6ed7ae7f-2591-5747-9fa0-933260aaaebf" :question/math-academy-id "e-12866" :question/problem "Solve the equation $-\\dfrac{z}{3}-\\dfrac 1 2 =\\dfrac 7 2$." :question/worked-solution "First, we apply the addition principle, adding\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{1}{2}\n$$\n\nto both sides:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} -\\dfrac{z}{3}-\\dfrac 1 2 &=\\dfrac 7 2 \\\\[5pt] -\\dfrac{z}{3} - \\dfrac 1 2+\\dfrac 1 2 &= \\dfrac 7 2+\\dfrac 1 2 \\\\[5pt] -\\dfrac{z}{3} + 0 &= \\dfrac 7 2+\\dfrac 1 2 \\\\[5pt] -\\dfrac{z}{3} &=\\dfrac 8 2 \\\\[5pt] -\\dfrac{z}{3} &=4 \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the multiplication principle. We multiply by $-1$ to get rid of the negative sign, and again by $3$ to get rid of the fraction.\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel} \\begin{aligned} -\\dfrac{z}{3} &=4 \\\\ (-1) \\cdot \\left(-\\dfrac{z}{3} \\right) &= (-1) \\cdot 4 \\\\[5pt] \\dfrac{z}{3} &=-4 \\\\[5pt] \\cancel{3} \\cdot \\dfrac{z}{\\cancel{3}} &= 3 \\cdot (-4) \\\\[5pt] z &=-12 \\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186055179 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186054657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82077653-3463-5132-b0a9-8376fdb47319" :knowledge-point/title "Solving Linear Equations that Involve Fractions"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a6831d18-43ec-5dd7-b0d7-b96de99de3d4" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052371} {:answer/id #uuid "e8799bb3-58d5-50d8-99ec-06232fb5986f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052372} {:answer/id #uuid "ff6b8afa-5a1c-569d-bf7b-19d0f2a18923" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052373} {:answer/id #uuid "3d27a309-0bbf-5fcd-9a6b-c774eac2658f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052374} {:answer/id #uuid "65763377-79b8-5e41-b68f-947b8ca32f35" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{20}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052375}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8ad4a929-789a-52ff-93db-ed9f973cda83" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186052370}] :question/id #uuid "b53aeb0c-2291-515b-8b32-fdcd601499c7" :question/math-academy-id "q-2540" :question/problem "If $\\frac{x}{5} + 2 = \\frac{2}{3}$, then $x =$"}]}
